SECTION 19 — FAIRNESS REVIEW AND ANTI-CHEATING SAFEGUARDS
=========================================================

Create an Interview Review feature for authorized reviewers.

Review whether:

* Questions are relevant to the job.
* Questions follow the approved interview plan.
* Core questions are consistent across candidates.
* Scoring criteria were defined in advance.
* Scoring criteria were changed without authorization.
* Scores have supporting evidence.
* Personal or discriminatory questions may have been asked.
* Relevant technical incidents occurred.
* Important evaluation steps were omitted.

Support analysis of authorized interview transcripts, submitted notes, and structured interview records.

If audio recording or transcription is implemented, obtain appropriate informed consent and clearly disclose its purpose, access rules, and retention period.

Do not claim to have analysed audio or video if the system has not actually received and processed it.

Use these review outcomes:

A. No obvious concern found in the available evidence.
B. Potential fairness concern requiring human review.
C. Insufficient evidence to assess.

Every concern must show:

* The observed issue.
* Supporting evidence.
* Relevant question, event, or timestamp when available.
* Severity.
* Confidence and limitations.
* Recommended review action.

Do not make definitive fairness or misconduct judgments from weak evidence.

## Anti-cheating controls

Implement appropriate controls such as:

* Authenticated interview sessions.
* Server-authorized joining.
* Scheduled access windows.
* Server-side answer submission.
* Server-side scoring where feasible.
* Submission timestamps.
* Audit logs for important events.
* Detection of repeated or suspicious submission patterns.
* Session-integrity event logging.
* Clear permitted-resource instructions.
* Candidate reporting of technical issues.

Do not automatically treat tab switching, connection loss, pauses, assistive technology, or unusual timing as proof of cheating.

Require human review before adverse decisions.

Do not implement covert surveillance, hidden recording, unauthorized microphone or camera access, or invasive monitoring.

If recording is implemented, clearly disclose it, obtain appropriate informed consent, show a recording indicator, restrict access, and support applicable retention and deletion requirements.

