SECTION 24 — FIREBASE SECURITY RULES
====================================

Security is mandatory.

Inspect the existing Firestore and Storage Security Rules before changing them.

Do not replace existing rules blindly.

Implement least-privilege access.

Requirements:

* Users can edit only their own permitted profile fields.
* Users cannot change their own privileged roles.
* Only authorized administrators or trusted backend processes can verify companies.
* Recruiters can manage only their authorized company records.
* Companies cannot read or modify another company's private records.
* Candidates can access only their own authorized applications and interviews.
* Recruiters can access applications for jobs they manage.
* Private resumes and certificates require appropriate authorization.
* Official quiz scores and interview results cannot be modified by unauthorized users.
* Hackathon submissions become immutable after the deadline unless an authorized exception exists.
* Interview records and scoring changes are traceable.
* Private feedback reports are restricted to authorized reviewers.
